    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d536">

                <pb facs="0529" n="525" sameAs="frus:frus1938v03/pg525"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.51/6599: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Hankow</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-03-23T16:00:00+08:00">March 23, 1938—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received March 23—2:32 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>170. Grant Forbes called on me today. He brought a letter from his [uncle]
                    Cameron Forbes.<anchor n="86" xml:id="d536-f1"/> I do not know whom he
                    represents but believe that he is working with and for a financial group of
                    which Jean Monnet<anchor n="87" xml:id="d536-f2"/> and T. V. Soong have been
                    dominating and moving spirits. Forbes stated that he had been discussing with
                    Kung possibilities of a material credit arrangement which I believe was based on
                    China’s holdings of silver, but that Kung had made conditions so difficult that
                    he thought his principals would not approve. Forbes stated he was awaiting reply
                    to a telegram. He suggested to me that American Government might be well advised
                    to grant Chinese forces aid in the form of munitions. I told Forbes that I saw
                    no chance of <pb facs="0530" n="526" xml:id="pg526"/> this; that furthermore I
                    had on all occasions attempted to make quite clear to the Chinese that they
                    could not expect any such aid from American sources.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
